1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,150
约 1.4 公斤，仅占体重的 2%
About 1.4 kg, just 2% of your body weight

2
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:06,350
约 860 亿个神经元
Around 86 billion neurons

3
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:09,550
却消耗全身约 20% 的能量
Yet it burns about 20% of your energy

4
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:12,750
它依靠分工明确的脑区协同运作
It runs on specialised regions working together

5
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:15,950
感知、记忆、情绪、决策……
Sensing, remembering, feeling, deciding…

6
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:19,150
分别由谁负责？
Who is in charge of what?

7
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:22,350
从脑区到前额叶皮层
From brain regions to the prefrontal cortex

8
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:25,550
第一章 · 认识大脑的主要脑区
Chapter 1 · The major brain regions

9
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:28,750
大脑皮层分为四个脑叶
The cerebral cortex has four lobes

10
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:31,950
下方还有小脑与脑干
Beneath sit the cerebellum and brainstem

11
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:35,150
思考、计划与自主运动的中枢
Hub of thought, planning and voluntary movement

12
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:38,350
后缘的初级运动皮层，指挥全身肌肉
Its rear strip, the motor cortex, commands your muscles

13
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:41,550
整合触觉、痛觉与身体位置感
Integrates touch, pain and body position

14
00:00:41,600 --> 00:00:44,750
还负责空间注意：知道东西“在哪里”
And spatial attention: knowing where things are

15
00:00:44,800 --> 00:00:47,950
处理声音、理解语言、参与记忆
Processes sound, language comprehension and memory

16
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:51,150
韦尼克区受损：说话流利，却难以理解
Wernicke's area damage: fluent speech, poor comprehension

17
00:00:51,200 --> 00:00:54,350
视觉中枢：初级视皮层 V1 所在地
The visual centre, home of primary visual cortex V1

18
00:00:54,400 --> 00:00:57,550
视觉信息由此分为“是什么”与“在哪里”两路
From here, vision splits into 'what' and 'where' pathways

19
00:00:57,600 --> 00:01:00,750
协调动作、维持平衡、学习运动技能
Coordinates movement, balance and motor skill learning

20
00:01:00,800 --> 00:01:03,950
只占脑重约 10%，却拥有约 80% 的神经元
About 10% of brain mass, yet ~80% of its neurons

21
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:07,150
由中脑、脑桥、延髓组成，连接脊髓
Midbrain, pons and medulla, linking brain to spinal cord

22
00:01:07,200 --> 00:01:10,350
自动调控呼吸、心跳与觉醒
Runs breathing, heartbeat and wakefulness on autopilot

23
00:01:10,400 --> 00:01:13,550
感觉信息进入皮层前的中继站
The relay hub for signals heading to the cortex

24
00:01:13,600 --> 00:01:16,750
除嗅觉外，几乎所有感觉都先经过这里
Nearly every sense except smell passes through here first

25
00:01:16,800 --> 00:01:19,950
仅约 4 克，掌管体温、饥饿与睡眠节律
Just ~4 g, it runs temperature, hunger and sleep cycles

26
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:23,150
通过垂体，调控全身的激素分泌
Through the pituitary, it steers the body's hormones

27
00:01:23,200 --> 00:01:26,350
把当下的经历写成长期记忆
Turns today's experiences into long-term memories

28
00:01:26,400 --> 00:01:29,550
H.M. 双侧海马大部切除后，记不住新经历
With most of both hippocampi gone, H.M. formed no new memories

29
00:01:29,600 --> 00:01:32,750
侦测威胁、触发恐惧的“警报器”
The alarm that detects threats and triggers fear

30
00:01:32,800 --> 00:01:35,950
让带有情绪的事件被记得格外牢
It makes emotional events stick in memory

31
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:39,150
有一个脑区，与“人之为人”关系最密切
One region is most tied to what makes us human

32
00:01:39,200 --> 00:01:42,350
它最晚发育成熟，一直持续到 20 多岁
It is among the last to mature, well into your 20s

33
00:01:42,400 --> 00:01:45,550
计划、专注、克制、抉择
Planning, focus, self-control, choice

34
00:01:45,600 --> 00:01:48,750
都离不开它
All of them depend on it

35
00:01:48,800 --> 00:01:51,950
第二章 · 大脑的指挥中心
Chapter 2 · The brain's command centre

36
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:55,150
位于额叶前部，运动相关区域之前
The front of the frontal lobe, ahead of the motor areas

37
00:01:55,200 --> 00:01:58,350
统筹注意、记忆与情绪，服务于目标
It coordinates attention, memory and emotion toward goals

38
00:01:58,400 --> 00:02:01,550
它可细分为多个功能亚区
It divides into specialised subregions

39
00:02:01,600 --> 00:02:04,750
位于额中回，对应布罗德曼 9 区与 46 区
Middle frontal gyrus, Brodmann areas 9 and 46

40
00:02:04,800 --> 00:02:07,950
工作记忆：在脑中暂存并加工信息
Working memory: holding and working with information

41
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:11,150
延迟任务中，神经元在等待期持续放电
In delay tasks, its neurons keep firing through the wait

42
00:02:11,200 --> 00:02:14,350
认知控制：制定计划，按规则切换任务
Cognitive control: making plans and switching rules

43
00:02:14,400 --> 00:02:17,550
位于额下回，紧邻外侧裂
Inferior frontal gyrus, just above the lateral fissure

44
00:02:17,600 --> 00:02:20,750
右侧额下回：叫停冲动，抑制反应
Right inferior frontal gyrus: stopping impulsive responses

45
00:02:20,800 --> 00:02:23,950
左侧 44/45 区即布洛卡区，负责言语产生
Left areas 44/45 form Broca's area, for speech production

46
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:27,150
还帮助从记忆中挑选、提取所需信息
It also selects and retrieves what you need from memory

47
00:02:27,200 --> 00:02:30,350
前额叶的最前端，在人类中相对更大
The very tip of the PFC, relatively enlarged in humans

48
00:02:30,400 --> 00:02:33,550
挂起主目标，先处理子任务，再切回来
It parks a main goal, handles a subtask, then returns

49
00:02:33,600 --> 00:02:36,750
元认知：评估“我有多确定”
Metacognition: judging how sure you are

50
00:02:36,800 --> 00:02:39,950
权衡探索新选项，还是利用旧经验
Weighing exploring the new against exploiting the known

51
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:43,150
位于额叶底面，就在眼眶上方
On the frontal lobe's underside, right above the eye sockets

52
00:02:43,200 --> 00:02:46,350
计算奖励价值：这对我值多少？
Computes reward value: what is this worth to me?

53
00:02:46,400 --> 00:02:49,550
规则一变，迅速更新预期（逆转学习）
Rapidly updates when rules flip: reversal learning

54
00:02:49,600 --> 00:02:52,750
嗅觉与味觉在此汇聚，形成“美味”的感受
Smell and taste converge here into the pleasure of flavour

55
00:02:52,800 --> 00:02:55,950
位于前额叶内侧下部，与内侧 OFC 部分重叠
Lower medial PFC, overlapping with the medial OFC

56
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:59,150
1848 年，铁棍贯穿盖奇头颅，他从此性情大变
1848: an iron rod changed Phineas Gage's personality

57
00:02:59,200 --> 00:03:02,350
躯体标记假说：情绪信号引导决策
Somatic marker hypothesis: emotional signals guide choices

58
00:03:02,400 --> 00:03:05,550
还参与调节恐惧，平复负面情绪
It also helps regulate fear and calm negative emotion

59
00:03:05,600 --> 00:03:08,750
环绕胼胝体前部，常被归入内侧前额叶
Curves around the front of the corpus callosum

60
00:03:08,800 --> 00:03:11,950
冲突监测：察觉“冲动”与“目标”打架
Conflict monitoring: noticing when impulse and goal collide

61
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:15,150
一出错，脑电立刻出现“错误相关负波”
Slip up, and an error signal (the ERN) fires within ~100 ms

62
00:03:15,200 --> 00:03:18,350
还编码疼痛有多“难受”，而不是痛在哪
It also encodes how much pain hurts, not where it hurts

63
00:03:18,400 --> 00:03:21,550
六个亚区，各司其职
Six subregions, each with its own job

64
00:03:21,600 --> 00:03:24,750
但它们并非单打独斗，而是组成网络
But none works alone: they form networks

65
00:03:24,800 --> 00:03:27,950
并与杏仁核、海马、丘脑紧密相连
And they are wired to the amygdala, hippocampus and thalamus

66
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:31,150
认识大脑，就是认识自己
Know your brain, know yourself

67
00:03:31,200 --> 00:03:34,350
图示已简化，非精确解剖比例
Diagrams are simplified, not to anatomical scale

68
00:03:34,400 --> 00:03:37,550
谢谢观看
Thanks for watching
